+## 1. William Caton's 1828 consent — “Jr” survives in the photographed typescript
+
+**STATUS:** found / partial  
+**RECORD:** Fauquier County Marriage Bonds and Returns, vol. 4, typed p.279; FamilySearch DGS 007578973, image 149/445. Bond 12 Jan 1829; consent 6 Dec 1828.  
+**URL:** https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-89XF-K9SG-S?view=fullText  
+**SOURCE INSPECTED:** user-supplied `Transcript (99).pdf`.
+
+Pertinent copied text identifies William as “my son William Caton,” followed by “Thomas Caton Jr (SEAL)”; another “Thomas Caton” appears in the witness line with James Payne (of Thos.) and Presley Johnson.
+
+**GRADE:** A/fact for what is visible on the photographed typescript; B/fact for the parent-child statement preserved by this derivative county copy; C/hypothesis for mapping either Thomas to a census Thomas.
+
+**CONFLICTS/LIMITS:** The suffix is not merely modern OCR, but the image is still a typescript rather than the original loose consent. It cannot support autograph comparison. It does not establish that the consenting father equals the 1830 man styled “Thomas Caton Jun.” C092 versus the identity assumptions behind C082/C193/C194 remains unresolved.
+
+## 2. T13 guardianship locator is wrong-county
+
+**STATUS:** found  
+T13 connects Gott's Fauquier guardian-bond work to FamilySearch catalog 642321, film 1689208 / DGS 8682856. That film is `Record of guardians, 1800–1868` for **Chatham County, North Carolina**, not Fauquier County, Virginia.
+
+**CORROBORATING URL:** https://www.werelate.org/wiki/Source:North_Carolina._County_Court._Record_of_Guardians%2C_1800-1868  
+**GRADE:** A/fact for the catalog mismatch.
+
+**RESEARCH CONSEQUENCE:** remove this film/DGS from Fauquier access instructions; a negative on it would be a wrong-county negative. John K. Gott, *Fauquier County, Virginia, Guardian Bonds, 1759–1871* (Heritage Books, 1990; ISBN 1556132735) remains a legitimate independent target, but its surname entries were not inspected.
+
+## 3. Fauquier Overseers/apprenticeship source is a real bounded target
+
