+## 5. 1810 Fauquier Thomas — counts corroborated, relationships are not
+
+**STATUS:** found  
+**RECORD:** published 1810 census transcription, Fauquier Co.  
+**LOCATOR:** NARA M252-68; p.263B line 11; handwritten p.398.  
+**TRANSCRIBER:** Jan Carter; proofreader Sandy Onbey.  
+**URL:** https://www.us-census.org/pub/usgenweb/census/va/fauquier/1810/pg0262a.txt
+
+**COUNTS:** male 45+ = 1; female 16–26 = 1; female 45+ = 1; no other members marked.
+
+**GRADE:** B/fact — independent published transcription of the same census, not a second primary record.
+
+**CONFLICT/CORRECTION:** C159 labels the older woman Thomas's wife and the younger woman his daughter, then infers a death/remarriage before 1820. The census states neither relationship.
+
+**GRADE C/hypothesis:** the younger woman could instead have been Thomas's wife and the older woman another relative. This is an alternative to test, not an identification of Aaron's mother.
+
+**RESEARCH CONSEQUENCE:** do not require Aaron's mother to come from an 1811–1819 marriage or require the bride to have been a widow. Retain pre-1810 and later-marriage possibilities until the women are identified independently.
